.TH SU 1
.SH NAME
su \- a shell as another user
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B su
.RI [ name ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B su
starts a shell as
.I name
(default root), with
.IR name 's
password; root needs none. Type
.B exit
to come back.
.PP
It only asks the accounts server,
.BR auth (8),
which checks the password and starts the shell as
.BR su 's
child;
.B su
waits for it. A login without a password (root) does not open an
encrypted home: only the user's password does.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The shell's, or 1 if refused.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR passwd (1),
.BR sh (1),
.BR auth (8)
